.TH SWAYDESK-NETWORK-POPUP 1 2026-11-14 "swaydesk 0.2.1" "Sway desktop components"
.SH NAME
swaydesk\-network\-popup \- network popup for Waybar
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swaydesk\-network\-popup
.SH DESCRIPTION
Turns networking and Wi\-Fi on and off, lists the wired connections, the VPNs and the Wi\-Fi networks, connects, disconnects and shows the details of the active connection. It talks to NetworkManager over D\-Bus.
.PP
Without NetworkManager on the bus, it talks to iwd (Wi\-Fi) and systemd\-networkd (the cable, state only). There are no VPNs, connection editor or networking switch then, and they are hidden.
.PP
With NetworkManager it never reads, receives or stores passwords: NetworkManager asks its secret agent (nm\-applet) for them. With iwd, which has no agent of its own, the open popup registers as iwd's agent: the password of a new network is typed in the popup and goes only in the D\-Bus reply to iwd. With the popup closed there is no agent, and iwd connects only to the networks it already knows. Enterprise (802.1X) networks need iwd's own provisioning file.
.PP
Running it again while the popup is open closes it, and opening it closes the other popups of the bar. Esc, clicking outside or switching workspace also closes it.
.PP
The session runs it under the name waybar\-network\-popup (a link in the package's helper directory to /usr/bin/swaydesk\-network\-popup); the process name is waybar\-network\-popup too.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Exit 0 at once without doing anything: the Python launchers use it to check that the binary and its libraries load.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/swaydesk/config.toml
The desktop configuration: language, accent color, GTK and icon themes, folder color, file manager, weather location and holidays.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR NetworkManager (8),
.BR nm\-applet (1),
.BR iwd (8),
.BR systemd\-networkd (8),
.BR swaydesk (7)
